# Digicom-ET USSDGW — Docker configuration.
#
# Copy to docker/.env and edit:  cp docker/.env.example docker/.env
# .env is gitignored and must never be committed (it holds site-specific paths and
# may hold an admin key). The swarm stack reads this file at deploy time.
#
# The Digicom-specific variant (env.digicom.example) lives only on the private
# `digicom` branch — never on public main.

# --- images ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tag every image with the git SHA it was built from. That is the rollback key:
# `docker service rollback` and `docker service update --image ussdgw:<sha>`.
USSDGW_IMAGE=ussdgw:latest
NGINX_IMAGE=ussdgw-nginx:latest
# The image built from docker/postgres/Dockerfile, NOT stock `postgres:16`.
# docker/build/build-images.sh builds all three images under one tag and asserts
# inside the postgres image that it carries docker-entrypoint-initdb.d/01-ussdgw.sh
# (which creates the `ussdgw` role + database, without which the gateway cannot
# start) and that it pins listen_addresses to loopback. Pointing this at a bare
# upstream `postgres:16` removes both: the gateway then fails with
# `FATAL: role "ussdgw" does not exist`, and 5432 binds on every interface of the
# host because every service here is on hostnet.
POSTGRES_IMAGE=ussdgw-postgres:latest

# --- operator configuration (plan.md R7) ----------------------------------------
# The directory the operator hands over. install-config.sh copies it into
# DATA_ROOT/configs ONCE and never overwrites it afterwards.
CONFIG_SRC=/srv/ussdgw/configs

# Where the build artifacts are staged (the builder's /out).
BUILD_ROOT=/srv/ussdgw-build
# Sources the operator audited. The builder mounts this read-only.
SOURCE_ROOT=/srv/ussdgw-build/src
# source mode: local (verify SHAs only) | git (clone at pinned SHAs)
SOURCE_MODE=local

# --- runtime storage ------------------------------------------------------------
# Bind-mounted, persistent, owned by uid 10001 (configs/logs/data) and 999 (pgdata).
DATA_ROOT=/srv/ussdgw

# --- resource profile ----------------------------------------------------------
# WHICH PROFILE YOU ARE ON IS THE MOST IMPORTANT SETTING IN THIS FILE.
#
#   TEST (default) - the Digicom test server and any small host. ~4 CPU / 6 GiB.
#       docker stack deploy -c docker/stack.yml -c docker/stack.test.yml ussdgw
#   5k  (production only) - capacity_5k_tps.md: 16 CPU / 64 GiB ussdgw +
#       12 CPU / 32 GiB postgres, on a 128 GiB / 32 CPU host.
#       docker/capacity/preflight-capacity.sh 5k      # REFUSES a host that is too small
#       docker stack deploy -c docker/stack.yml \
#           -c docker/capacity/stack.capacity-5k.yml ussdgw
#
# The test server has very little RAM and CPU. Running the 5k overlay there is NOT a
# graceful downgrade: Swarm schedules against reservations the host cannot honour and
# the JVM gets OOM-killed mid-MAP-dialog. 5 000 TPS is a production goal, not a test
# server goal - and a config that asks for 64 GiB is not evidence it was achieved.
DEPLOY_PROFILE=test

# Heap for the TEST profile. AGENTS.md heap rule: a shared or small host cannot spare
# more than 4g to one container.
USSD_XMS=1g
USSD_XMX=4g
# Hard container limit for swarm. Must exceed USSD_XMX with room for netty direct
# buffers and SCTP native memory, or the JVM is OOM-killed mid-dialog.
USSDGW_MEM_LIMIT=6g

# --- secrets --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set these with swarm secrets, NOT here:
#   printf '<db-password>' | docker secret create ussdgw_db_password -
#   printf '<admin-key>'   | docker secret create ussdgw_admin_key -
# USSD_ADMIN_API_KEY below is a lab default only. In production the gateway reads
# /run/secrets/ussdgw_admin_key and this value is ignored.
USSD_ADMIN_API_KEY=ussd-admin

# --- public URL -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Used for the admin UI's generated links and for AS callbacks. Never 0.0.0.0.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost

# --- node -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# The gateway is pinned to the node the carrier peers whitelist. Set by host-prep.sh:
#   docker node update --label-add ussdgw=true $(hostname)